finding: 1. src/cli/publish-fly.ts:174–178,385–387 — Post-deploy inventory fails open on invalid rows. Only the array wrapper and its length are checked, so [null] or [{}] counts as a real resource. In a scratch copy on e91bc4d, changing the missing-resource fixtures in publish-fly-target.node.ts:350–366 from [] to [null] made all three deploy promises resolve, including when neither list identified a resource. 2. src/cli/publish-fly.ts:196–226 — On either refusal path the report can mislabel invalid rows: e.g. a volume row with id "vol_extra" and size_gb -1 is counted and printed with negative monthly spend because Number.isFinite(-1) is true. Missing/invalid IDs are handled only when formatting a refusal, and the regex accepts arbitrary tokens rather than recognizing provider IDs. Inventory validation needs to distinguish unreadable rows from real resources while preserving usable evidence from either list.
